==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{etydate|1846}} From {{der|en|fr|psychiatrie}}, from {{der|en|ML.|psychiatria}}. {{surf|en|psych-|alt1=psych-|-iatry}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/saɪˈkaɪ.əˌtɹi/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-psychiatry.wav |Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|+}}

# {{lb|en|medicine}} The branch of [[medicine]] that focuses on {{w|mental health|mental and behavioral health}} by subjectively [[diagnose#Verb|diagnosing]], treating, or preventing mental disorders ([[mental illness#Noun|mental illnesses]]) and [[behavior#Noun|behavioural]] conditions.

